      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "DE LA RENTA NZ (2) scored at Tamworth two runs ago before having her colours lowered when seventh at her latest appearance over 1609m at Menangle, beaten 22 metres. Likely to get all the favours from this nice draw. Finds a suitable assignment and can turn things around. A LITTLE DILEMMA (1) settled close to the pace then surged to the lead and finished the race off well to score in a 1609m race at Tamworth last start, arriving 3.5 metres ahead of her rivals at her first run back from a layoff. A nice draw on the front line should ensure a cosy run. Meets a similar line up so she is capable of getting the job done again. BRONSKI ROYAL (6) is better than his last-start eighth over 2125m at Penrith. SKY CITY NZ (5) disappointed last time when seventh over 1609m at this track. Can bounce back.",
